> And remove magic whistles from the game?

No, without magic whistles it would be unbearably
tedious to keep a pet past about dungeon level six.
I have played games where I never found one of the
blessed things, but that's much more apt to make
the game less fun than to genuinely make it more
challenging.

Okay, yes, with a magic whistle you could steal
from a shop even if the shopkeeper blocked the
door.  But it would be harder, because you would
have to be outside and thus would have a harder
time knowing when the pet had picked stuff up.
Of course, the shopkeepers *could* also be
programmed to notice if a monster teleports or
is whistled out of the shop with unpaid merch,
but the fact that hostility is tracked only relative
to the player creates issues there.  Neither the
shopkeeper nor Kops could easily be set to
pursue a particular thieving monster and yet
be peaceful to the player without adding some
rather significant additional monster-behavior
code for them, I think.  Hmmm...


